WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:07.400
For teams paying for coding AI, specialist gaps can still consume time and limited usage allowances.

2
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:14.900
PairWork lets teams contribute what they do best, earn credits, and request help from another specialist.

3
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:22.400
People review each result. Credits are earned through work; they cannot be purchased, cashed out, or transferred freely.

4
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:29.900
Each exchange needs no per-job crypto transfer. We are testing whether that makes collaboration easier.

5
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:37.400
Pro subscriptions could offer team selection and priority matching. Enterprise networks are a later possibility, not a current product.

6
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:44.900
Illustration: one thousand members at fifteen hundred yen per month would mean one point five million yen in monthly revenue, before costs.

7
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:52.400
This is not sales or profit. Next we must test repeat use, work quality, willingness to pay, and real integrations.

8
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.900
The playable browser demo shows one exchange. Solana Devnet recording and in-product skill integration still need verification.
